{
  "work_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense",
  "source_path": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense.json",
  "source_language": "oge",
  "target_language": "eng",
  "provenance": {
    "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04": {
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "prompt_version": "bulk-2026-10-12",
      "date": "2026-11-04",
      "script": "__main__"
    }
  },
  "translations": [
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.28.4",
      "source_sha256": "ed3ff52c74c10d4d",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "[?] from terror of him the guards trembled and became like dead men."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.28.5",
      "source_sha256": "de4fc570dfae9219",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The angel answered and said to the women: \"Do not be afraid, for I know that you are seeking Jesus who was crucified."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.28.6",
      "source_sha256": "da3e957ca8707605",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He is not here, but he has risen, as he said. Come and see, and see the place where they laid"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.28.7",
      "source_sha256": "02d0fbfc43aef7ca",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "him. And go quickly and tell his disciples that he has risen. And behold, he is going before you to Galilee; there you will see him. Behold, I have told"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.28.8",
      "source_sha256": "f11386d714858447",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "you.\" And they went away quickly from the tomb with fear and great joy, and ran to tell his disciples."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.28.9",
      "source_sha256": "938c5c60ed60fc73",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And behold, Jesus met them and said: \"Rejoice.\" And they, and they came up and took hold of his feet and worshipped"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.28.10",
      "source_sha256": "88cdd25618bf3061",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "him. Then Jesus said to them: \"Do not be afraid. Go and tell my brothers to go to Galilee, and there they will see me.\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.28.11",
      "source_sha256": "3391aea522321ddd",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And they went, and behold, some of the guard came into the city and told the chief priests all that"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.28.12",
      "source_sha256": "b68c9f36970236b9",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "had happened. And they gathered with the elders and took counsel. They gave a large sum of silver to the soldiers"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.28.13",
      "source_sha256": "3c45e4c312cf9292",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and said: \"Say this: 'His disciples came by night and stole him away while we were sleeping.'"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.28.14",
      "source_sha256": "4b88a4146b6e98d6",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And if the governor hears of this, we will persuade him and keep you free from trouble.\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.28.15",
      "source_sha256": "87acff35c9e065e2",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And they took the silver and did as they had been taught by them. And this story has spread among the Jews to this very day."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.28.16",
      "source_sha256": "0997f7a105caa482",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And the eleven disciples went to Galilee, to the mountain where Jesus had directed"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.28.17",
      "source_sha256": "5a3c1b89fce82f36",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "them. And they saw him and worshipped him, but some doubted."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.28.18",
      "source_sha256": "91943df397e2ab0b",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And Jesus came up to them, spoke to them and said: \"All authority in heaven and on earth has been given to me."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.28.19",
      "source_sha256": "1dd3fa90c967cb57",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Go and make disciples of all the nations, and baptize them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.28.20",
      "source_sha256": "e177a6117ec905f4",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And teach them to keep all that I have commanded you. And behold, I am with you all the days, until the end of the world.\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Mark.16.2",
      "source_sha256": "10fea6bb9fd26556",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Reading from the chapter of Mark of the holy Gospel. And very early, at dawn on the first day of the week, they came to the tomb, just as the sun was rising."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Mark.16.3",
      "source_sha256": "9a0b9bb58ab896df",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And they were speaking to one another. They said [?]: \"Who will roll the stone away for us from the door of the tomb?\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Mark.16.4",
      "source_sha256": "e621bc16ea95e163",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And they looked and saw that the stone had been rolled away, and it was very large."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Mark.16.5",
      "source_sha256": "d1463d499f1d690e",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And when they went into the tomb, they saw a young man sitting on the right side, dressed in a white robe, and they were alarmed."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Mark.16.6",
      "source_sha256": "6e2816c4b8e6a560",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And he said to them: \"Do not be alarmed. You are seeking Jesus the Nazarene, who was crucified. He has risen; he is not here. Behold the place where they laid him."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Mark.16.7.s1",
      "source_sha256": "f595b5949518c856",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But go and tell his disciples and Peter"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Mark.16.7.s2",
      "source_sha256": "ed48c5b843977c79",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "that, behold, he is going before you to Galilee; there you will see him, as he told you.\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Mark.16.8",
      "source_sha256": "dd1b846460fa0780",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And when they heard this, they came out and fled from the tomb, for they were trembling and amazed. And they said nothing to anyone, for they were afraid."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.1.s1",
      "source_sha256": "e8317ef40cb58f5d",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Reading from the chapter of the holy Gospel of Luke. Now on the first day of the week, at dawn, they came early to the tomb."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.1.s2",
      "source_sha256": "91a8eb124628893c",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And they were bringing the spices they had prepared, and some others were with them."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.2",
      "source_sha256": "b5805859781c8111",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And they found the stone rolled away from the tomb."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.3",
      "source_sha256": "bc1ad2456fda0410",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "When they went in, they did not find the body of the Lord Jesus."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.4",
      "source_sha256": "ce3a0462fd15b3bf",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And while they were puzzling over this, behold, two men stood by them in shining garments."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.5",
      "source_sha256": "540844d35ad114c3",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And as they were afraid and bowed their faces to the ground, the men said to them, \"Why do you seek the living one among the dead"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.6",
      "source_sha256": "264b4c9b83ea612a",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "[among the dead]? He is not here, but has risen. Remember how he told you while he was still in Galilee, and said,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.7",
      "source_sha256": "f073745a5c932642",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "'The Son of Man must be handed over into the hands of sinful men to be crucified, and on the third day rise.'\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.8",
      "source_sha256": "bc92e20ee814c58c",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And they remembered words"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.9",
      "source_sha256": "a4e4adfaacdf7c26",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "these words, and they returned and told these things to the eleven and to all the others."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.10",
      "source_sha256": "ecdb7cc6007b1bbd",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Now they were Mary Magdalene, and Joanna, and Mary the mother of James. And the other women with them were telling this to the apostles, and"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.11",
      "source_sha256": "2ca7e5e8761d581f",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "their words seemed to them like idle talk [?], and they did not believe them."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.12",
      "source_sha256": "ab41ee495499229a",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But Peter got up and ran to the tomb. He stooped down and saw the linen cloths lying there by themselves, and he went away by himself, marvelling at what had happened."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.13",
      "source_sha256": "4720fbf8e84f2681",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And behold, on that same day two of them were going to a village a hundred and sixty stadia from Jerusalem, whose name was Emmaus, whose name was Evmaoz."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.14",
      "source_sha256": "cb5fd3ce7331af2d",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And they were talking with each other about everything that had happened."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.15",
      "source_sha256": "bf3bde6ab95e90b9",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And while they were talking and discussing, Jesus himself came near to them and went along with them."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.16",
      "source_sha256": "f1a85ab934bf0f66",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But their eyes were held, so that they could not recognize him."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.17",
      "source_sha256": "c705c7fd29ab83ed",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And he said to them, \"What are these words that you are arguing about with each other as you walk, and why are you sad?\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.18",
      "source_sha256": "7f656de787d8e1ad",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "One of them, whose name was Cleopas, answered and said to him, \"Are you the only stranger in Jerusalem who does not know what has happened there in these days?\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.19.s1",
      "source_sha256": "e14f2e9069e4b69c",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And he said to them, \"What things?\" And they said to him, \"About Jesus the Nazarene,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.19.s2",
      "source_sha256": "c23a80b338c9caf0",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "who was a man, a prophet mighty in deed and in word before God and all the people,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.20",
      "source_sha256": "19d43fc1a6b0b463",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and how the chief priests and our rulers handed him over to be condemned to death, and crucified him."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.21",
      "source_sha256": "3e2429a7c00aea70",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But we were hoping that he was the one who would redeem Israel. And besides all this, it is now the third day since these things happened."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.22",
      "source_sha256": "c64289f85d3f1568",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But some women of ours have also astonished us. When they went to the tomb at dawn"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.23",
      "source_sha256": "f97620c1d8fb464c",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and did not find his body, they came and said that they had even seen a vision of angels, who told them that he is alive."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.24",
      "source_sha256": "7acc57d988303520",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And some of those who were with us went to the tomb, and they found it just as the women had said. But him they did not see."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.25",
      "source_sha256": "9a458738e7830158",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And he said to them: \"O foolish ones, slow of heart to believe all that the prophets spoke!"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.26",
      "source_sha256": "4a88d6f67f05f038",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Was it not necessary for the Christ to suffer these things, and to enter into his glory?\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.27",
      "source_sha256": "8ebacbecc95acb38",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And beginning from Moses and the prophets, he explained to them what was said about himself in all the scriptures."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.28",
      "source_sha256": "121261d857a6f52b",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And they drew near to the village to which they were going, but he made as though he would go farther."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.29",
      "source_sha256": "5a8314c91b54f466",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "They urged him, saying: \"Stay with us, for it is evening, and the day is now far spent.\" And he went in to stay"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.30",
      "source_sha256": "4262b875d13b67cb",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "with them. And when he sat down with them, he took bread, blessed it, broke it, and gave it to them."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.31",
      "source_sha256": "7fa54b8a365261ae",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And their eyes were opened, and they recognized him; and he vanished from their sight."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.32.s1",
      "source_sha256": "f00cfdedf64cb1b9",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And they said to one another: \"Did not our hearts burn within us while he talked to us on the road,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.32.s2",
      "source_sha256": "4a23fd7e1a3026e9",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and while he explained the scriptures to us?\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.33",
      "source_sha256": "624200bdc9cb219e",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And they rose up that same hour and returned to Jerusalem, and they found the eleven gathered together, and those who were with them,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.34",
      "source_sha256": "1b0cc664cd0e699e",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "saying: \"The Lord has truly risen, and has appeared to Simon.\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.24.35",
      "source_sha256": "1032e62ff108265d",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And they told what had happened on the road, and how he was made known to them in the breaking of the bread."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.1.s1",
      "source_sha256": "746aeadaf64ac442",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Reading from the holy Gospel of John, from the chapter [?]. On the first day of the week Mary Magdalene came to the tomb early, while it was still dark,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.1.s2",
      "source_sha256": "1b7e569c0b1cd1ae",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and she saw that the stone had been taken away from the door of the tomb."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.2",
      "source_sha256": "1ef7b676ecd5fd48",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "So she ran and came to Simon Peter and to the other disciple, the one whom Jesus loved, and said to them: \"They have taken the Lord out of the tomb, and I do not know where they have laid him.\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.3",
      "source_sha256": "90f0bb58c3f6ffd8",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Then Peter went out with the other disciple, and they went toward the tomb."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.4",
      "source_sha256": "a30c702f7a1ae8d0",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Both of them were running together, but the other disciple ran ahead, faster than Peter, and reached the tomb first."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.5",
      "source_sha256": "e3f6d7f9d5d2cd5e",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He looked into the tomb and saw the linen cloths lying there, but he did not go in."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.6",
      "source_sha256": "ff807fc387be0ca8",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Then Simon Peter also came after him and went into the tomb, and he saw the linen cloths lying there, and the cloth"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.7",
      "source_sha256": "2102e49dd082b85e",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "that had been on his head, not lying with the linen cloths but folded up by itself in a separate place."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.8",
      "source_sha256": "9c850a3945b970dc",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Then the other disciple, who had reached the tomb before Peter, also went in; and they saw and believed,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.9",
      "source_sha256": "89991af02b171332",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "for they did not yet understand the scripture, that he must rise from the dead."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.10",
      "source_sha256": "d3283b9a845f7add",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Then the disciples went back again to their homes."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.11",
      "source_sha256": "846d4c6f228ad793",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But Mary stood weeping outside by the tomb; and as she wept, she looked into the tomb."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.12",
      "source_sha256": "bc82f943c26d8f82",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And she saw two angels clothed in white garments, sitting one at the head and one at the feet, where the body of Jesus had lain."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.13",
      "source_sha256": "db5e4b7f245bb53a",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And the angels said to her, \"Woman, why are you weeping?\" And she said to them, \"Because they have taken my Lord away from the tomb, and I do not know where they have laid"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.14",
      "source_sha256": "59df64fc5880ef85",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "him.\" When she had said this, she turned around and saw Jesus standing, and she did not know that it was Jesus. Jesus said"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.15.s1",
      "source_sha256": "e042d02f35d7290a",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "to her, \"Woman, why are you weeping? Whom are you looking for?\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.15.s2",
      "source_sha256": "d6d11461b27a16ec",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "She thought that he was the gardener. She said to him, \"Lord, if you have taken him away, tell me where you have laid him, so that I may take him away.\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.16",
      "source_sha256": "d8f4f33908d053f4",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Jesus said to her, \"Mary.\" She turned and said to him in Hebrew, \"Rabbouni,\" which means \"Teacher.\" And she ran forward to touch him."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.17.s1",
      "source_sha256": "54e35c798b9a2377",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Jesus said to her, \"Do not touch me, for I have not yet ascended to my Father. Go to my brothers and say to them,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.17.s2",
      "source_sha256": "ef9c2d93165c4451",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "'I am ascending to my Father and your Father, to my God and your God.'\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.18",
      "source_sha256": "a7f313beeb6aaef5",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Mary Magdalene came to tell his disciples that she had seen the Lord, and that he had said these things to her."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.19.s1",
      "source_sha256": "063e615d1a6bc7ba",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "On the day of [?] (ahusebay), in the evening, after \"Joyful Light,\" they recite. It says: Psalm 149: \"Sing to the Lord a new song; his praise is in the assembly of the saints.\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.19.s2",
      "source_sha256": "ae3c7cc6130a696e",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Gospel of John, from the chapter [?]. And it was evening on that day, the first day of the week, and the doors were shut where the disciples were, hidden for fear of the Jews."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.19.s3",
      "source_sha256": "548accb298c07309",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Jesus came and stood among them and said to them, \"Peace be with"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.20",
      "source_sha256": "3c908b902fa3e247",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "you.\" And when he had said this, he showed them his hands and his side. The disciples rejoiced when they saw"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.21",
      "source_sha256": "235f442345bf9962",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "the Lord. Jesus said to them again, \"Peace be with you. As the Father has sent me, so I also send you.\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.22",
      "source_sha256": "e59757b7d0412daf",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And when he had said this, he breathed on them and said to them, \"Receive the Holy Spirit."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.23",
      "source_sha256": "11f503363ad3ffab",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "If you forgive anyone's sins, they are forgiven them; if you retain anyone's sins, they are retained.\" But Thomas,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.24",
      "source_sha256": "482dd00dbec6db37",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "one of the twelve, who was called the Twin, was not with them when Jesus came."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.25.s1",
      "source_sha256": "31eabb60fba236ad",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The disciples told him, \"We have seen the Lord.\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.25.s2",
      "source_sha256": "29497bb76d25b491",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But he said to them, \"Unless I see in his hands the mark of the nails, and put my finger into the mark of the feet,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.25.s3",
      "source_sha256": "3b78d821486b743b",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and put my hand into his side, I will never believe.\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Iadgari.WPasch_1_d2.s1",
      "source_sha256": "89737bbc796e0d3b",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Christ God, the King, who was born of a virgin without seed, before whom the powers of heaven tremble: sing to him, you priests; you peoples, exalt him above all forever."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Iadgari.WPasch_1_d2.s2",
      "source_sha256": "04c7ba9f6f2c29dd",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He who by the will of the Father came down from heaven to earth, released [us from] [?] our sins, and willingly stretched out his hands on the cross: enlighten [us], O Benefactor."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.26.s1",
      "source_sha256": "e607f897cf38e651",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "On the day of [?] (ahusebay) of Easter, in the evening, at the hour of the choir [?]: Psalm 149: \"Sing to the Lord a new song; his praise is in the assembly of the saints.\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.26.s2",
      "source_sha256": "2851e7f062d46cb9",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Gospel of John, from the chapter [?]. And after eight days the disciples were again in one place,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.26.s3",
      "source_sha256": "c9ec8b92f1bf39ac",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and Thomas was with them. Jesus came in while the doors were shut, stood among them, and said to them, \"Peace be with you.\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.27",
      "source_sha256": "4c595d2ecc4b8a86",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Then he said to Thomas, \"Bring your fingers here and see my hands; and bring your hand and put it into my side. And do not be unbelieving, but believe.\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.28",
      "source_sha256": "4e72e452e6847e42",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Thomas answered and said to him, \"My Lord and God"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.29",
      "source_sha256": "4060a88bb0275c8d",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "of mine!\" Jesus said to him, \"Because you have seen me, you have believed. Blessed are those who have not seen and"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.30",
      "source_sha256": "068a1a23de3a201e",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "have believed.\" Jesus also did many other signs before his disciples, which are not written in this book. But these"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#John.20.31",
      "source_sha256": "ef0249da273e827c",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "are written so that you may believe that Jesus is the Christ, the Son of God, and that, believing, you may have life in his name."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Gal.6.14.s1",
      "source_sha256": "9967e698c9ea4441",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The Apostolic Epistle of Paul to the Galatians. But for me, let there be no boasting except in the cross of our Lord Jesus Christ,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Gal.6.14.s2",
      "source_sha256": "01ce52f6e60f0c64",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "through which the world has been crucified to me, and I to the world. For neither"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Gal.6.15",
      "source_sha256": "29eaa62b50a2a2a4",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "is circumcision anything, nor uncircumcision, but a new creation."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Gal.6.16",
      "source_sha256": "b9f4b9a06f348ecf",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And as for those who walk by this rule, peace be upon them, and mercy, and upon the Israel of God. From now on"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Gal.6.17",
      "source_sha256": "42aa0933f5d9fd98",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "let no one cause me trouble, for I bear in my body the sufferings of the Lord Jesus."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Gal.6.18",
      "source_sha256": "b5dd8a14844afad5",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit, brothers. Amen."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.24.29.s1",
      "source_sha256": "3c0db7d0d97f14b0",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The Gospel of Matthew, chapter [?]. Immediately after the tribulation of those days the sun will be darkened,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.24.29.s2",
      "source_sha256": "833394100daefeed",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and the moon will not give its light, and the stars will fall from heaven, and the powers of the heavens will be shaken."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.24.30.s1",
      "source_sha256": "15012660b2b13e5a",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And then the sign of the Son of Man will appear in heaven. And then all the tribes of the earth will mourn,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.24.30.s2",
      "source_sha256": "07776b483fcc348e",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and they will see the Son of Man coming with the clouds of heaven, with power and great glory."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.24.31.s1",
      "source_sha256": "0b4f027177dac344",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And he will send out his angels with a great trumpet, and they will gather his elect from the four winds, from one end of heaven to its other end."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.24.31.s2",
      "source_sha256": "40c0dbd0c234d2a0",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But learn this parable from the fig tree: when its branches become tender and the leaves come out, you know that summer is near."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.24.33",
      "source_sha256": "506a224e8cce4eeb",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "So also you: when you see all these things, know that it is near, at the doors."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Iadgari.WPasch_1_c2",
      "source_sha256": "5f5bed74da4986f7",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Sing praise to the consubstantial Trinity."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.24.34",
      "source_sha256": "481b22e5a2c7b315",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Truly I say to you that this generation will not pass away until all these things"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Matt.24.35",
      "source_sha256": "e9c536cc3cd9a3fe",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "take place. Heaven and earth will pass away, but my words will not pass away."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Rom.15.25",
      "source_sha256": "faf8f797ebe87978",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The Apostolic Epistle of Paul to the Romans. But now, behold, I am going to Jerusalem to minister to the saints."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Rom.15.26",
      "source_sha256": "4f8320c448d7187b",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For Macedonia and Achaia have been pleased to make some contribution for the poor among the saints who are in Jerusalem. They were pleased to do it,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Rom.15.27",
      "source_sha256": "01840690c47b6ef8",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and indeed they are in their debt. For if the Gentiles have shared in their spiritual things, they ought also to minister to them in bodily things."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Rom.15.28",
      "source_sha256": "6fb922e39fe08937",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "So when I have completed this and have sealed this fruit of theirs, I will set out by way of you."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Rom.15.29",
      "source_sha256": "9308c643b9a8ee8c",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 7,
      "text": "...to Spain. And I know that when I come to you, I will come in the fullness of the blessing of Christ."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.12.32.s1",
      "source_sha256": "f0a21291f8c3bd4b",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 7,
      "text": "Gospel of Luke, from the chapter [?]. Sell your possessions and give alms."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.12.32.s2",
      "source_sha256": "fb17b0e05d7944f8",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 7,
      "text": "Make for yourselves a treasure that does not grow old, an unfailing treasury in the heavens,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.12.32.s3",
      "source_sha256": "37ff3961003103e1",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 7,
      "text": "where no thief comes near and no moth destroys. Where [?]"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.12.31",
      "source_sha256": "742c59de20355722",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 7,
      "text": "Do not be afraid, little flock, for your Father has been pleased to give [?] the kingdom."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.12.33",
      "source_sha256": "5215da10375d560f",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 7,
      "text": "[?] your treasure is, there also will your heart be."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-khanmeti-lectionary/lectionarium-gracense#Luke.12.34",
      "source_sha256": "48c3f73cdda40eb5",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 7,
      "text": "Let your loins be [?]"
    }
  ]
}
